# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Makefile build output (make build/run/demo)
/bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Release artifacts built by scripts/release-build.sh (make release-dry-run).
# Generated per-build and attached to GitHub Releases; never committed.
dist/

# Local developer runtime state (task 062): platform database and the
# discovery file naming the running endpoint. Project-local and disposable —
# `rm -rf .trustvian` ends the environment.
.trustvian/

# The root-level CLI binary, if you build it with `go build` rather than
# `make build` (which writes to /bin/). Anchored with a leading slash, like
# /bin/ above: an unanchored `trustvian` matches every path component with that
# name — including cmd/trustvian/ — which silently ignores new source files
# there. scripts/gitignore_test.go fails if that regresses.
/trustvian

# The processor module's fixture binaries, if you build them with `go build`
# without -o. Anchored for the same reason /trustvian is: `agent-producer`
# unanchored would also match processor/cmd/agent-producer/, silently ignoring
# new source files in it.
/processor/agent-producer
/processor/demo-producer
/processor/trustvian-collector

# The examples' build output: `go build` in examples/<name> writes an
# executable named <name> beside main.go. One per program, anchored for the
# reason /trustvian is; scripts/gitignore_test.go fails when a program has
# no entry, or when any native executable is tracked.
/examples/ai-agent/ai-agent
/examples/ai-agent-security/ai-agent-security
/examples/alert-webhook/alert-webhook
/examples/basic/basic
/examples/configured-engine/configured-engine
/examples/credential-misuse/credential-misuse
/examples/external-destination/external-destination
/examples/frequency-abuse/frequency-abuse
/examples/persistent-baseline/persistent-baseline
/examples/unexpected-dependency/unexpected-dependency
